New adventuring skill: bolster.

1) Bolster works armor up toward the most it could ever be, spending
   soulstone charges.
   - There is no set length.  It runs until the piece reaches its ceiling,
     the stone runs dry, or something stops you.

2) The ceiling is the tier's own maximum, opening fully at level 35.
   - Heavy armor can reach 55; clothing tops out well short of that.

3) Every attempt costs charges whether it lands or not.
   - The cost rises with the piece, so a fine piece is dear to improve.
   - A level ten stone pays a tenth of what a level one stone pays for the
     same work.

4) Difficulty is read fresh each attempt from how far along the piece
   already is.
   - The last stretch of a heavy piece is the hardest work there is.
   - Monk's clothing is comparatively easy to finish.

See HELP BOLSTER and HELP SOULSTONE.
